Z||000021||Tonker||07-12-2001||12:28 AM||||DarkLord: I agree the MR2 mkII's look a bit nicer and certainly have the performance to match their looks, but it would probably be more fair to compare the styling vs. the mk.I's which were out at the same time. I personally think the Fiero wins hands down, but I know a lot of ppl who would disagree. And I'd be quite happy to own a mkI in addition to my Fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I also think the Fiero has aged pretty gracefully. I don't see that many new cars that I would swap my Fiero for.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Well unless they have a really good resale value... Sure they're a bit more rounded now but the GTs and Formulas don't look so typically 80's. I asscociate them more with an early to mid 90's style. Hmm, I'm ranting aren't I? Yeah, I'm ranting.  <P>Oh and just to get back on topic I love that MR2 shogun front end.||||reg||1
